This K version exposes the intended composition mechanism directly: a separately proved reachability claim can be marked trusted for a later proof run. I’ll first retain the independent `#Top` proof of `binary-loop`, then use that exact claim—unchanged—as a derived lemma for the two entry claims. This adds no unproved execution summary.
